From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs8550-ayn-thor: correct haptics LRA/ERM flag

The shared AYN device tree claims the haptics actuator is an ERM with
"qcom,use-erm = <0x01>", while the same node carries "qcom,lra-period-us"
and LRA-specific brake and waveform properties, so the node contradicts
itself.  Thor ships a linear resonant actuator, so the ERM claim is wrong
for this board.

The flag is not cosmetic.  In the qcom-hv-haptics driver it decides three
things:

  - whether haptics_parse_lra_dt() runs at all, so "qcom,lra-period-us"
    and the LRA brake configuration are only parsed when the flag is clear;
  - haptics_load_constant_effect() calling
    haptics_enable_autores(chip, !chip->config.is_erm), so a set ERM flag
    disables LRA auto resonance for every DIRECT_PLAY upload;
  - the drive and brake waveforms, which are forced to WF_NO_MODULATION
    when the flag is set instead of the "qcom,drv-sig-shape" sine shape.

The result is a silent motor.  An FF_CONSTANT upload and its play request
both succeed, so evdev reports no error and userspace sees a working
device, but the actuator is driven without auto resonance and without
modulation and moves too little to feel.  Userspace haptics libraries
cannot work around this, because the driver accepts the request and only
the hardware behaviour is wrong.

The driver reads the flag with of_property_read_bool(), which tests
presence, not value: overriding the property to <0x00> still leaves the
driver in ERM mode (the kernel warns "Read of boolean property
'qcom,use-erm' with a value" at boot).  Delete the property in the Thor
board file so the driver falls back to the LRA path for this board only.
The shared AYN default is left untouched for the other AYN devices, whose
actuators this change has not been measured on.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -164,5 +164,15 @@ multi-ledl4 {
 	};
 };
 
+&pm8550b_hv_haptics {
+	/*
+	 * Thor's actuator is an LRA, not an ERM.  The driver reads
+	 * "qcom,use-erm" with of_property_read_bool(), which tests
+	 * presence, not value: overriding it to <0x00> still leaves the
+	 * driver in ERM mode.  Delete the property to use the LRA path.
+	 */
+	/delete-property/ qcom,use-erm;
+};
+
 &display_panel {
 	compatible = "chipone,icna3520";
 
